# JK2 NPC AI architecture (reference)

Full doc: [docs/jk2-npc-ai-architecture.md](docs/jk2-npc-ai-architecture.md)

## Core model

- **Move vs shoot:** separate `AImove` / `shoot` flags each attack tick; `squadState` gates feet, LOS/`NPC_ShotEntity` gates fire. Commander assigns goals only.
- **No NPC alert enum:** use `enemy`, investigate state, `squadState`, and `AEL_*` on `alertEvents`.
- **Wake allies:** `G_SetEnemy` → `G_AngerAlert` → `G_AlertTeam` (512/256). Not `squadname`. Shares enemy pointer only.
- **Groups:** `AI_GetGroup` rebuilds a frame clipboard (morale, last-seen, `numState[]`). `ST_Commander_*` runs once per group per frame; **each member gets their own** `NPC_FindCombatPoint`, not one squad waypoint.
- **Combat points:** `point_combat` near fight; pool is **512 units around enemy**. `CP_COVER` = hidden from enemy, `CP_CLEAR` = can shoot. `CP_CLOSEST`/`CP_APPROACH`/`CP_FLANK` cause rushes and behind-player paths. Relaxation drops flags to `CP_ANY`.

## JKG

Stormtrooper logic: `AI_Stormtrooper_JKG.cpp` when `JKG_AI`. Senses/groups/combat points are stock. Debug: `sv_cheats 1` then `g_jkgDebugNpcState`. Nav/CPs: stock `nav show …` (see docs/jk2-npc-ai-architecture.md).

## Do not assume

- Officer `group->commander` does not issue orders to the whole squad each frame.
- `SQUAD_TRANSITION` = running to an assigned combat point, not a special squad mode.
- `BS_STAND_AND_SHOOT` for troopers does not replace `squadState` for combat posture.
